{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISION (operator-approved, 2026-08-30): **Option 1 — edge fix via nginx `proxy_redirect` prefix-restore.**\n\nScope for this ticket:\n- Add a per-location `proxy_redirect` to the `/review/` block that restores the `/review/` prefix on the app's self-referential absolute redirects (post-a61d the app emits `https://$host/<route>`, so the rule is `proxy_redirect https://$host/ https://$host/review/;`), coexisting with a61d's existing scheme rules and the restated `proxy_redirect default;`.\n- Pin it with a structural test over the RENDERED nginx config (reuse a61d's `_render_nginx()` harness in `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`), asserting `/review/health/`-style redirects retain the `/review/` prefix AND that the existing prefix-STRIPPING request path is unchanged (`GET /review/health` still reaches the app as `/health`).\n- Add a guard comment + a test that pins the review-bot's redirect surface as same-app-only, so the documented residual (a future off-`/review/` absolute redirect would be wrongly prefixed) is caught if it ever changes.\n\nRationale + evidence: the review-bot is a plain `uvicorn rebar.review_bot.app:app` FastAPI service with NO `--root-path`, NO `RedirectResponse`, and no cross-host redirects — its only absolute redirects are Starlette trailing-slash 307s to its own routes. So the broad same-host rewrite has no legitimate redirect to corrupt today, and `proxy_redirect`'s host-anchored match cannot touch a cross-host redirect. This directly fixes the observed `Location` symptom regardless of app internals and reuses a61d's per-location + structural-test pattern.\n\nRejected Option 2 (app-side `root_path`/APIRouter mount): known FastAPI/Starlette gotcha — `root_path` does not reliably prepend the prefix to `redirect_slashes` `Location` headers, so it may not fix the observed symptom without larger app changes; bigger blast radius + more verification.\n\nDeploy note: the code lands through Gerrit now; LIVE VALIDATION (AC4) is satisfied by the SAME operator edge-deploy that clears a61d's AC5 (gated on 1d1b's detect-signal + operator apply). Do NOT deploy or touch the box; do not block on live validation.\n\nDispatching a background /rebar-debug agent under this scope."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788110544788464229,"uuid":"980cdace-c1f8-4c4d-8419-84d7e3de60ca"}